---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="GDPR Compliance — Mithra" description="Mithra's GDPR compliance commitments: data subject rights, lawful basis, cross-border transfers, and our Data Processing Agreement.">
  <Navigation />

  <!-- Dark header -->
  <section class="pt-24 pb-12 bg-ibm-gray-100">
    <div class="max-w-8xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 pt-8">
      <p class="text-ibm-blue text-sm font-medium tracking-wider uppercase mb-3">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-light text-white mb-3">GDPR Compliance</h1>
      <p class="text-ibm-gray-40 text-sm">Last updated: May 27, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Content -->
  <section class="py-16 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-8xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">

        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Mithra Technologies S.A. de C.V. ("Mithra") is committed to complying with the General Data Protection Regulation (EU) 2016/679 ("GDPR") in all aspects of our operations that involve the personal data of individuals in the European Economic Area (EEA) and the United Kingdom. This page describes our GDPR commitments, the roles we play in data processing, and how data subjects can exercise their rights.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">1. Mithra's Role Under GDPR</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Mithra operates in two distinct capacities depending on the context of the data involved:
        </p>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Data Processor.</strong> When Mithra processes personal data on behalf of enterprise customers as part of delivering the platform, Mithra acts as a <em>data processor</em>. In this capacity, we process data only according to the documented instructions in the applicable Data Processing Agreement (DPA) and the relevant Order Form. The customer remains the <em>data controller</em> and is responsible for the lawfulness of the processing instructions they give us.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Data Controller.</strong> When Mithra collects and processes personal data about its own customers, prospects, and website visitors for its own operational purposes (such as account management, billing, marketing communications, and security logging), Mithra acts as the <em>data controller</em>. This processing is governed by our <a href="/privacy" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">2. Lawful Basis for Processing</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">As a data controller, Mithra relies on the following lawful bases under GDPR Article 6:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-ibm-gray-70 mb-4">
          <li><strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Contract performance (Art. 6(1)(b)):</strong> Processing necessary to perform the contract with our customers — account provisioning, service delivery, billing, and customer support.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Legitimate interests (Art. 6(1)(f)):</strong> Processing necessary for our legitimate business interests, including fraud prevention, security monitoring, and product analytics, where these interests are not overridden by data subjects' rights.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Consent (Art. 6(1)(a)):</strong> Where we send optional marketing communications or deploy non-essential cookies, we rely on freely given, specific, and informed consent, which you may withdraw at any time.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Legal obligation (Art. 6(1)(c)):</strong> Processing required to comply with applicable law, including tax, financial reporting, and data breach notification obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">3. Data Subject Rights</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Under GDPR, individuals whose personal data we control have the following rights. All requests should be directed to <a href="mailto:dpo@mithra.ai" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">dpo@mithra.ai</a>. We will respond within one calendar month (extendable by two months for complex requests).
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-ibm-gray-70 mb-4">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Right of Access (Art. 15):</strong> You may request confirmation of whether we process your personal data and, if so, a copy of that data along with information about how it is used. Requests can be submitted via email to <a href="mailto:dpo@mithra.ai" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">dpo@mithra.ai</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Right to Erasure / Right to be Forgotten (Art. 17):</strong> You may request deletion of your personal data where it is no longer necessary for the purposes for which it was collected, where you have withdrawn consent, or where processing is unlawful. We will honor requests unless retention is required by law.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Right to Data Portability (Art. 20):</strong> Where processing is based on consent or contract and carried out by automated means, you may request your data in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format (JSON or CSV). You may also request direct transfer to another controller where technically feasible.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Right to Restriction of Processing (Art. 18):</strong> You may request that we restrict processing of your data while you contest its accuracy, while a legitimate interests objection is assessed, or if you require the data for legal claims but we no longer need it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Right to Object (Art. 21):</strong> You may object to processing based on legitimate interests or for direct marketing. Where you object to direct marketing, we will stop processing immediately. For other objections, we will cease processing unless we can demonstrate compelling legitimate grounds.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Right not to be subject to automated decisions (Art. 22):</strong> We do not make purely automated decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects on individuals without human review.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Note: If you are an end user of a Mithra enterprise customer's deployment, your rights requests regarding data processed on that customer's behalf should be directed to the customer (data controller). We will assist the customer in fulfilling these obligations as required under our DPA.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">4. Cross-Border Data Transfers</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Mithra is headquartered in Mexico City, Mexico. Where personal data of EEA residents is transferred to our infrastructure, we ensure appropriate safeguards are in place in accordance with GDPR Chapter V:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-ibm-gray-70 mb-4">
          <li><strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs):</strong> For transfers to our group entities and sub-processors in jurisdictions without an adequacy decision, we rely on the European Commission's 2021 Standard Contractual Clauses. Copies of our SCCs are available on request.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">Adequacy decisions:</strong> Where the European Commission has issued an adequacy decision for the destination country, we rely on that decision to lawfully transfer data.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ibm-gray-100">EU-US Data Privacy Framework:</strong> Mithra and our US-based sub-processors (where applicable) participate in, or contract with participants of, the EU-US Data Privacy Framework (DPF), which provides a lawful mechanism for transatlantic data transfers following the 2023 adequacy decision.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Enterprise customers with strict data residency requirements may configure their account to store and process data exclusively within the EEA. See our <a href="/security" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">Security page</a> for available regions.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">5. Data Protection Officer</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Mithra has appointed a Data Protection Officer (DPO) who is responsible for overseeing our GDPR compliance program, serving as the primary point of contact for data subjects and supervisory authorities, and advising on data protection impact assessments.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-ibm-gray-70 mb-4">
          <li>Email: <a href="mailto:dpo@mithra.ai" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">dpo@mithra.ai</a></li>
          <li>Mail: Data Protection Officer, Mithra Technologies S.A. de C.V., Paseo de la Reforma 250, Mexico City, Mexico</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">6. EU Representative</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          As a non-EU organization that offers services to EEA residents and monitors their behavior, Mithra is required under GDPR Article 27 to designate an EU representative. We are in the process of establishing our EU representative office in Amsterdam, Netherlands, which is expected to be operational by Q3 2026.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Until the Amsterdam office is operational, EEA-based data subjects and supervisory authorities should direct all GDPR inquiries to our DPO at <a href="mailto:dpo@mithra.ai" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">dpo@mithra.ai</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">7. How to Lodge a Complaint</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          If you believe that Mithra has not handled your personal data in compliance with GDPR, you have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority. You may contact:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-ibm-gray-70 mb-4">
          <li>The supervisory authority in the EU member state where you reside or work.</li>
          <li>The supervisory authority where the alleged infringement took place.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          A directory of EU supervisory authorities is available at <a href="https://edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/about-edpb/members_en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">edpb.europa.eu</a>. We encourage you to contact us first so we can attempt to resolve your concern directly.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ibm-gray-100 mt-10 mb-4">8. Data Processing Agreement (DPA)</h2>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Enterprise customers who require a Data Processing Agreement to fulfill their own GDPR obligations may request our standard DPA at any time. Our DPA covers:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-ibm-gray-70 mb-4">
          <li>The subject matter, nature, purpose, and duration of the processing.</li>
          <li>Mithra's obligations as a data processor, including sub-processor management and security measures.</li>
          <li>Procedures for handling data subject requests forwarded by the customer.</li>
          <li>Data breach notification timelines and procedures.</li>
          <li>Assistance with data protection impact assessments (DPIAs).</li>
          <li>Standard Contractual Clauses as an annex for cross-border transfers where required.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-ibm-gray-70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          To request a copy of our DPA, email <a href="mailto:dpo@mithra.ai" class="text-ibm-blue hover:underline">dpo@mithra.ai</a> with the subject line "DPA Request" and your company name. We will respond within 5 business days.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
